cross join (values
    ('Neon coffee sign', 'Look for glowing tubes spelling out coffee-related words, usually in red or pink, that brighten up the window, especially cool at dusk.', 'Identify a glowing neon sign with coffee-related text or imagery. The sign must emit visible light with neon tubing visible in the frame.', 'common'::public.item_rarity, 'Neon tubes emit light by ionizing gas inside glass tubes at around 3,600 degrees—hotter than lava but safe because they hold minimal energy.', 'https://cejsntpvctcgezrluvql.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/collection-item-images/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/wiki-cache/d520d29634d1bb41.jpg', 0),
    ('Vintage tin advertisements', 'Hunt for old metal signs with faded coffee brand logos and retro graphics, often weathered and slightly rusty, leaning against the glass.', 'Locate metal tin signs or boxes with aged, printed advertising graphics. Look for visible text, brand names, or decorative imagery on metal surfaces.', 'uncommon'::public.item_rarity, 'Lithographed tin signs from the 1920s-50s often contained chromated copper arsenate (CCA) as a pigment, making authentic vintage signs technically toxic.', 'https://cejsntpvctcgezrluvql.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/collection-item-images/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/wiki-cache/6b91326032052e2f.jpg', 1),
    ('Potted plants and flowers', 'Spot green plants or fresh flowers placed on windowsills or hanging near the glass to add life and softness to the display.', 'Detect living plants or flowers displayed in pots or containers within the window. Include flowering plants, green foliage, or planted arrangements.', 'common'::public.item_rarity, 'Pothos and snake plants release oxygen at night while absorbing CO2, unlike most plants, making them effective for improving air quality in dim café corners.', 'https://cejsntpvctcgezrluvql.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/collection-item-images/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/wiki-cache/019f3bb28d4b5ab3.jpg', 2),
    ('Menu boards and chalkboards', 'Find hand-written or printed menus on dark boards showing coffee drinks and prices, often decorated with drawings or handwritten notes.', 'Find chalk-written or printed menus displayed on boards. Look for text listing food, drinks, or prices on a visible board surface.', 'common'::public.item_rarity, 'Chalk dust can damage espresso machine components and grinders if it circulates in the air near exposed equipment—many cafés avoid chalk for this reason.', 'https://cejsntpvctcgezrluvql.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/collection-item-images/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/wiki-cache/46bb89990f706adb.jpg', 3),
    ('Espresso machine display', 'Look for shiny chrome or stainless steel espresso machines visible through the window, usually with pressure gauges and steam wands gleaming.', 'Spot an espresso machine positioned visibly in the window. It must show the machine''s body, group heads, portafilter, or steam wands.', 'common'::public.item_rarity, 'Group heads on espresso machines reach 200°F but the water inside is hotter—boilers maintain 250-280°F to generate the steam pressure needed for extraction.', 'https://cejsntpvctcgezrluvql.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/collection-item-images/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/wiki-cache/b8661f5ee549315b.jpg', 4),
    ('Pastry showcase case', 'Search for a glass display case filled with croissants, donuts, and pastries arranged neatly, tempting people walking by.', 'Identify a glass display case containing baked goods, pastries, or desserts. The case must show pastries visible behind or within glass.', 'common'::public.item_rarity, 'Curved glass in display cases is weaker at edges than flat glass due to stress concentration, which is why they sometimes shatter without impact.', null, 5),
    ('Hanging light fixtures', 'Notice pendant lights or lanterns suspended from above inside the window area, casting interesting shadows on the displays below.', 'Detect light fixtures suspended from above or mounted overhead. Include pendant lights, hanging lamps, or ceiling-mounted lighting.', 'common'::public.item_rarity, 'Edison bulbs used in vintage café displays produce only about 5% of their energy as light—the other 95% becomes heat, making them inefficient but visually warm.', 'https://cejsntpvctcgezrluvql.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/collection-item-images/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/wiki-cache/6adc05a24d7f0176.jpg', 6),
    ('Window decals and typography', 'Look for painted or vinyl letters and designs directly on the glass, including café names, opening hours, or decorative words.', 'Locate text, letters, or graphic decals applied directly to the window glass. Include painted or vinyl lettering with visible text or logos.', 'common'::public.item_rarity, 'Glass etching for window decals uses hydrofluoric acid, which bonds permanently to silica in glass—unlike paint, it cannot peel or wear off.', 'https://cejsntpvctcgezrluvql.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/collection-item-images/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/wiki-cache/f3e84f1dfdc5805e.jpg', 7),
    ('Barista tools on shelves', 'Spot organized displays of grinders, tampers, portafilters, and milk jugs arranged on shelves or hooks visible through the window.', 'Find coffee-making tools displayed on shelves: portafilters, tampers, grinders, milk jugs, or other barista equipment arranged visibly.', 'uncommon'::public.item_rarity, 'Tampers made from stainless steel conduct cold so efficiently that espresso grounds stick to them—wooden handles exist primarily to prevent this adhesion.', null, 8),
    ('Retro café furniture', 'Look for vintage chairs, small tables, or stools inside the window display area, styled from past decades with worn charm.', 'Identify vintage-style seating or tables visible in the window display. Look for period chairs, bistro tables, or classically styled furniture pieces.', 'uncommon'::public.item_rarity, 'Vinyl upholstery used in 1950s diner seating contains phthalates that leach out faster at higher temperatures, which is why café seating near heat degrades quicker.', 'https://cejsntpvctcgezrluvql.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/collection-item-images/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/wiki-cache/fd59fdec438b75b1.jpg', 9),
    ('Coffee bean sacks', 'Find burlap or canvas bags labeled with origin names like ''Ethiopian'' or ''Brazilian,'' stacked or leaning in a corner of the display.', 'Spot burlap sacks or bags filled with coffee beans. The sacks must show coffee beans or bean imagery clearly visible in the display.', 'uncommon'::public.item_rarity, 'Burlap coffee sacks absorb moisture from air, which causes beans inside to lose flavor—they''re primarily used for storage before roasting, not display.', 'https://cejsntpvctcgezrluvql.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/collection-item-images/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/wiki-cache/76f8ee02a92e767c.jpg', 10),
    ('Framed artwork and posters', 'Look for paintings, prints, or vintage coffee-themed posters hanging on walls visible through the window glass.', 'Find framed pictures, prints, posters, or artwork hung on walls or displayed in the window. The frame and artwork must be clearly visible.', 'common'::public.item_rarity, 'UV-protective glass used in café displays transmits 99% of light while blocking the wavelengths that fade artwork and vintage posters.', 'https://cejsntpvctcgezrluvql.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/collection-item-images/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/wiki-cache/dad9d5a16b5d6d5f.jpg', 11),
    ('Decorative mirrors', 'Spot mirrors of various sizes and frames reflecting the interior light and creating depth in the window display.', 'Locate mirrors with decorative frames or ornamental borders displayed in the window. The mirror surface and frame must be visible.', 'uncommon'::public.item_rarity, 'Mirrors in cafés reflect heat from lights and windows back into the space, potentially raising ambient temperature by 2-3 degrees on sunny days.', 'https://cejsntpvctcgezrluvql.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/collection-item-images/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/wiki-cache/e27c8379cb3eb1b6.jpg', 12),
    ('String lights and garland', 'Notice warm-toned fairy lights or twine with hanging decorations draped along the top or sides of the window frame.', 'Detect strands of decorative lights or garland draped in the window. Include fairy lights, decorative strings, or floral garland arrangements.', 'uncommon'::public.item_rarity, 'Warm white LEDs on string lights produce wavelengths around 2700K—the same hue as candlelight, which is why they feel more nostalgic than cool white lights.', 'https://cejsntpvctcgezrluvql.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/collection-item-images/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/wiki-cache/497812642c234bd0.jpg', 13),
    ('Takeaway cup stack display', 'Look for colorful paper coffee cups stacked in towers or pyramids, sometimes with the café logo or design printed on them.', 'Identify stacked disposable coffee cups arranged as a display. Show cups stacked vertically or horizontally with visible cup logos or designs.', 'rare'::public.item_rarity, 'Stacked paper cups can develop static charge through friction, causing ink and dust to cling irregularly—this is why cup stacks sometimes appear spotted.', 'https://cejsntpvctcgezrluvql.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/collection-item-images/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/wiki-cache/7c1d0d899528eaa8.jpg', 14)
